VISION_ANSWER=**1. Header and navigation**
- Same “role-model” sidebar label, “Runtime overview” page title, and top-right theme icon.
- Sidebar sections and order match: Overview selected, Studio, Local, Remote, Models, Router, Observe, Connect, System, Learning.
- Lower sidebar differs: production lists `chatgpt/gpt-8-astra 32`, two `DeepSeek V4.1 Flash_ 32` rows, and `chatgpt/gpt-6.1-sol 4`; rebuilt lists `Claude 3.7 Sonnet 0`, `gpt-5.4 0`, and `GPT-4.1 Mini Fast 0`.
- `CACHE no live samples` is the same. Router endpoint differs: production `127.0.0.1:3456/v1` / `baseline.remote-only`; rebuilt `127.0.0.1:3458/v1` / `-`.

**2. Main content blocks and cards/tables**
- Filter row labels and order match; `Day` is selected in both.
- `Breakdown` differs: production shows truncated `By endpoint vari...`; rebuilt shows `Total`.
- Model pool title, description, axes (`Quality`, `Cost`, `Speed`), and candidate-table header match.
- Production model pool has four candidate rows with numeric route scores; rebuilt has three rows with `—` scores.
- Production candidate names: `deepseek-flash (High)`, `deepseek-flash (Max)`, `gpt-5.1-sol`, `gpt-6-astra`. Rebuilt names: `openai/gpt-4.1-mini-fast`, `claude-3.7-sonnet`, `gpt-5.4`.
- Production shows a `Selected` label on the first candidate; rebuilt shows no selected label.
- Production plot has four spread-out markers; rebuilt has three markers clustered near the center/Cost side.
- Token usage section is populated in production: teal filled area, grid, x-axis times `00:00`–`24:00`, three legend entries, and the note `36 row(s) in this slice do not support inputTokens.`
- Rebuilt token usage section is empty: `No data`, tiny `1 tokens / 0.5 tokens / 0 tokens` axis, only `Input tokens` and `Output tokens` in the legend, and `No token-bearing requests have been recorded yet.`
- Cache efficiency trend heading/description match. Production shows the top of its chart with `8874k`, `100%`, and lines; rebuilt shows only the heading/description area in the screenshot.

**3. Typography and wording**
- Typography appears broadly consistent: same sans-serif UI font, heading/body sizing, muted descriptions, and small uppercase labels.
- Wording differences are mainly in the breakdown value, candidate names/scores/telemetry, token-usage empty state, and router endpoint status.
- Production candidate telemetry includes values such as `S100`, `S34`, `S9`, `S3`; rebuilt shows `S–` for all three and no `No live telemetry` row.

**4. Colours and theme**
- Both use the same dark near-black theme, dark sidebar, subtle borders, light text, and grey secondary text.
- Selected navigation state, buttons, and dropdown styling match.
- Production token usage has a teal filled area; rebuilt has no filled data. Candidate marker colours differ with the data: production uses blue/orange markers; rebuilt shows orange, blue, and green markers.

**5. Spacing and layout**
- Overall layout matches: fixed sidebar, same main-content column, same stacked card structure, and aligned filter row.
- Rebuilt shows a visible vertical page scrollbar on the far right; production does not show one in the screenshot.
- The rebuilt sidebar model list has fewer rows, leaving a different lower-sidebar distribution.
- The rebuilt token usage card is visually much emptier due to the missing plot and grid.

**6. Missing or extra**
- Missing from rebuilt versus production: fourth model row, numeric route scores, `Selected` indicator, production telemetry values, populated token usage chart, `Total tokens` legend entry, production note about unsupported input tokens, visible cache chart data, and `baseline.remote-only`.
- Extra/different in rebuilt: `Total` breakdown selection, `No data` token chart state, `No token-bearing requests have been recorded yet.`, endpoint dash, and visible page scrollbar.

